What does "persistent" mean?

Persistent = something that stays/remains even after a reboot.

Imagine you have an EBS disk:

EC2
 │
 └── EBS Volume
       │
       └── /data-ebs

You mounted the EBS volume manually:

sudo mount /dev/nvme1n1 /data-ebs

Now /data-ebs is accessible.

