=> Why we'll use /dev/disk/by-id/

Normally you might use UUID in /etc/fstab.

But in your lab, the original EBS and snapshot-restored EBS are cloned filesystems, so they can have the same filesystem UUID.

Therefore, for these two EBS volumes, using the AWS volume-specific by-id path is safer.

